# The SHA-256 of each trace tools/lemsim.py writes for levelN.txt against the
# committed fixture - the EXPECTED trace, pinned. The traces themselves are
# 720 KB of text and are regenerated by apps/lemmings/build.sh every build
# (0.2 s), so what is committed is the script that drives them and the hash
# that says the reference has not moved. A deliberate change to tools/lemsim.py,
# to a script or to the fixture recommits the line it moves.
